From: psyche <hkjeon13@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 14:51:32 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] Prefetch gate and up weights during the attention and
 norm kernels

Decode at one row is latency bound, and the gate/up dispatch is the one
kernel that waits on memory bandwidth (3.5 MB per layer). Extra blocks
appended to the QK score, AV and first merge-norm launches touch one word per
cache line of those weights, so the gate/up kernel finds them in L2. The extra
blocks only load; native tests rerun the attention and merge-norm comparisons
with prefetch blocks attached.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
